  "problem": "Write down the missing parts of a parametrization of our shell below.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r(x,\\theta )=\u27e8x,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\u27e9,\\,x\\in [0,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083460/assets/56a380b075d10862170ed9c9a45c07dddff3eaef1ea9fb3109a61cc3d27b5ac4.png)\n\n \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [a,b]$ has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\u27e8x,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \u27e9,\\,x\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(x)=2{x}^{2}\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [0,1].$\n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=\u27e8x,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \u27e9,\\,x\\in [0,\\,1],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$",
